{"judgments": [
  {"clause_id": "c001", "issues": [
    {"issue": "\"Authorized University official\" is undefined, so which employees may demand identification is left open. The provision also gives no consequence for an official who fails to reciprocate on request.", "type": 1, "prob": 0.07}
  ]},
  {"clause_id": "c002", "issues": [
    {"issue": "\"Replaced as soon as possible\" fixes no deadline and no benchmark against which delay could be measured. The distinction between a \"damaged\" card (free) and a \"lost\" card (fee) is likewise undefined.", "type": 1, "prob": 0.06}
  ]},
  {"clause_id": "c003", "issues": [
    {"issue": "The enumerated privileges (check cashing, elections, athletic events, library, campus technologies) are closed with \"etc.\", leaving the reach of the catch-all to ejusdem generis argument. \"Properly entitled\" is also undefined by any other provision.", "type": 1, "prob": 0.11}
  ]},
  {"clause_id": "c004", "issues": [
    {"issue": "\"Influencing\" another student to violate a standard has no boundary and is far broader than the neighboring verbs \"enticing\" and \"enlisting\". A court would have to decide whether mere influence, without solicitation, is sanctionable.", "type": 1, "prob": 0.12}
  ]},
  {"clause_id": "c005", "issues": [
    {"issue": "The sentence \"communicating information important requests, updates, policies\" is ungrammatical — a word or comma is missing — so what the e-mail account is the primary means of communicating is unclear. \"Maintain currency with the use of\" the account also states no measurable duty.", "type": 1, "prob": 0.14}
  ]},
