  ]},
  {"clause_id": "c035", "issues": [
    {"issue": "\"Appropriate posting materials that will not cause damage\" is judged after the fact and by no stated standard. The provision names no approving authority for non-residential spaces beyond a cross-reference.", "type": 1, "prob": 0.08}
  ]},
  {"clause_id": "c036", "issues": [
    {"issue": "\"Only sidewalks may be chalked\" cannot be squared with the later sentence barring chalking \"in areas where it cannot be washed away by the rain\", which assumes covered areas might otherwise be chalkable. \"Inappropriate\" chalked messages is also an undefined ground for removal.", "type": 1, "prob": 0.12}
  ]},
  {"clause_id": "c037", "issues": [
    {"issue": "\"Inappropriate use of property\" is an undefined catch-all appended to specific wrongs like vandalism and theft. The extension to \"personal and public property that surrounds the campus\" has no geographic limit.", "type": 1, "prob": 0.11}
  ]},
  {"clause_id": "c038", "issues": []},
  {"clause_id": "c039", "issues": [
    {"issue": "\"Explicit permission\" for storage closets, utility rooms and roof areas does not identify who may grant it or in what form. The general duty to observe \"University guidelines and policies\" incorporates unnamed documents.", "type": 1, "prob": 0.09}
  ]},
  {"clause_id": "c040", "issues": [
    {"issue": "\"Mistreatment of animals, trees, or plantings\" is undefined and gives no threshold — picking a flower and injuring an animal fall in the same words. No intent requirement is stated.", "type": 1, "prob": 0.07}
  ]},
  {"clause_id": "c041", "issues": []},
  {"clause_id": "c042", "issues": [
    {"issue": "The protected-class list here (adding ancestry, religious creed, ethnic origin, Vietnam Era Veteran and \"any other category protected by law\") differs from the list in 2.7 and again from the list in 7.3. Which enumeration defines a chargeable discrimination offense cannot be settled from any one of them.", "type": 2, "prob": 0.15}
  ]},
  {"clause_id": "c043", "issues": [
    {"issue": "Harassment is \"regarded as\" occurring when conduct has \"the purpose or effect of unreasonably interfering\" with education or work, with no severity or pervasiveness requirement and no statement of whose perception governs. Because a single unwelcome remark can have that \"effect\", the boundary of the offense is left to case-by-case construction.", "type": 1, "prob": 0.24}
  ]},
  {"clause_id": "c044", "issues": [
    {"issue": "The list is expressly non-exhaustive (\"includes, but is not limited to\") and several entries — \"leering\", comments that \"would otherwise tend to be degrading\" — have no objective content. Whether conduct outside the enumerated examples can constitute sexual harassment, and by what test, is open.", "type": 1, "prob": 0.20}
  ]},
  {"clause_id": "c045", "issues": [
    {"issue": "The closing sentence — the University \"may take action on conduct that it deems to be inappropriate, regardless of whether it rises to the level of a violation of law\" — makes the University's own view of inappropriateness the operative standard. Combined with \"This is not an exhaustive list\", the provision states no boundary a student could rely on.", "type": 1, "prob": 0.22}
  ]},
  {"clause_id": "c046", "issues": [
    {"issue": "This retaliation rule protects only persons who complain of harassment or discrimination or cooperate in such an investigation, while 2.14 forbids anything \"that could be construed as retaliation\" for any good-faith report to Public Safety or the conduct process. The two prohibitions differ in trigger and breadth and are cross-referenced to each other as if identical.", "type": 2, "prob": 0.11}
  ]},
  {"clause_id": "c047", "issues": [
