  ]},
  {"clause_id": "c053", "issues": [
    {"issue": "\"In a timely manner\" and \"not reported in a timely fashion\" fix no limitations period, yet untimeliness is a ground for refusing to refer a case. There is no benchmark against which the delay of a report could be measured.", "type": 1, "prob": 0.22},
    {"issue": "The statement that disciplinary action \"may be implemented only through the report of a violation to the [DSRCS]\" cannot be squared with 22.1, 22.3 and 22.4, under which the Dean may remove, suspend, or dismiss a student with no report at all. Which route is exclusive is unresolved.", "type": 2, "prob": 0.19}
  ]},
  {"clause_id": "c054", "issues": [
    {"issue": "The subject matter suited to mediation is a non-exhaustive list (\"includes, though is not limited to\") that does not exclude allegations under Section 3 or 7, although 3.0, 7.0 and 22.6 require that such allegations be adjudicated by the Special Examiner's Process. Whether a sexual misconduct allegation may be mediated instead cannot be answered from either provision alone.", "type": 2, "prob": 0.19}
  ]},
  {"clause_id": "c055", "issues": [
